# Plan: Step 9b — Reorder Pages via Drag and Drop (Split Mode)

## Context

Split mode already supports page reordering via up/down buttons (Step 9a). Step 9b adds drag-and-drop as a more direct alternative. `@dnd-kit/core`, `@dnd-kit/sortable`, and `@dnd-kit/utilities` are already installed but unused.

The only file that needs changing is `frontend/src/components/SplitMode/ThumbnailPanel.tsx`. The `onMovePage(fromPos, toPos)` callback already exists and handles the state mutation correctly.

## Approach

Use dnd-kit's `SortableContext` + `useSortable` for each page item in the virtual list, plus a `DragOverlay` that floats above the panel while dragging.

**Key challenge:** TanStack Virtual only renders visible items, but `SortableContext` needs all item IDs. Solution: pass the full `pageOrder` array as `items` to `SortableContext`; `useSortable` is only called for rendered items, which is fine.

**Auto-scroll:** `DndContext` auto-scrolls the nearest scrollable ancestor when the pointer nears the edge. This handles drag-to-scroll without extra configuration, so non-rendered items become droppable as the list scrolls.

## Implementation

### 1. Add state and sensors inside `SplitThumbnailPanel`

```ts
const [activeId, setActiveId] = useState<number | null>(null)
const sensors = useSensors(useSensor(PointerSensor, { activationConstraint: { distance: 8 } }))
```

The 8px activation constraint ensures clicks on rotate/skip/gap-zone buttons are not intercepted by the drag sensor.

### 2. New local `SortablePageItem` component

Wraps `PageThumbnail` only (not `GapZone`). Applies `useSortable` transform and makes the dragged item transparent (0 opacity) while the `DragOverlay` floats in its place.

```tsx
function SortablePageItem({ id, children }: { id: number; children: React.ReactNode }) {
  const { setNodeRef, transform, isDragging, attributes, listeners } = useSortable({ id })
  return (
    <div
      ref={setNodeRef}
      style={{ transform: CSS.Transform.toString(transform), opacity: isDragging ? 0 : 1 }}
      {...attributes}
      {...listeners}
    >
      {children}
    </div>
  )
}
```

### 3. Wrap the virtual list in `DndContext` + `SortableContext`

```tsx
<DndContext
  sensors={sensors}
  collisionDetection={closestCenter}
  onDragStart={({ active }) => setActiveId(active.id as number)}
  onDragEnd={handleDragEnd}
>
  <SortableContext items={pageOrder} strategy={verticalListSortingStrategy}>
    <div style={{ height: virtualizer.getTotalSize(), position: 'relative' }}>
      {virtualItems.map(vItem => {
        // headers unchanged
        // page items: wrap PageThumbnail in SortablePageItem; GapZone stays outside
        return (
          <div key={vItem.key} style={{ position: 'absolute', top: vItem.start, ... }}>
            <SortablePageItem id={page}>
              <PageThumbnail ... />
            </SortablePageItem>
            {!isLastPage && <GapZone ... />}
          </div>
        )
      })}
    </div>
  </SortableContext>
  <DragOverlay>
    {activeId !== null && (
      <PageThumbnail
        src={pageCache.getSrc(pdfPath, activeId)}
        pdfPath={pdfPath}
        page={activeId}
        thumbHeight={thumbHeight}
        isSelected={false}
        isSkipped={skipped.has(activeId)}
        rotation={rotations.get(activeId) ?? 0}
        isHovered={false}
        label={String(activeId)}
        onClick={() => {}}
        onRotate={() => {}}
        onToggleSkip={() => {}}
      />
    )}
  </DragOverlay>
</DndContext>
```

`DragOverlay` renders into a portal so it floats above the panel correctly regardless of DOM nesting.

### 4. `handleDragEnd`

```ts
const handleDragEnd = ({ active, over }: DragEndEvent) => {
  setActiveId(null)
  if (!over || active.id === over.id) return
  const fromPos = pageOrder.indexOf(active.id as number)
  const toPos = pageOrder.indexOf(over.id as number)
  if (fromPos !== -1 && toPos !== -1) onMovePage(fromPos, toPos)
}
```

Reuses the existing `onMovePage(fromPos, toPos)` in `SplitMode/index.tsx` — no changes needed there.

## Imports to add

```ts
import { DndContext, DragOverlay, PointerSensor, closestCenter, useSensor, useSensors } from '@dnd-kit/core'
import type { DragEndEvent } from '@dnd-kit/core'
import { SortableContext, useSortable, verticalListSortingStrategy } from '@dnd-kit/sortable'
import { CSS } from '@dnd-kit/utilities'
```

## Split points during drag

Split points are stored by positional index in `pageOrder`. Dragging a page across a split point moves it into the adjacent section — consistent with how up/down buttons already behave.

## Files changed

- `frontend/src/components/SplitMode/ThumbnailPanel.tsx` — only file that changes

## Verification

1. Open a multi-page PDF in Split mode
2. Drag a thumbnail — confirm it lifts out of the list and follows the cursor
3. Drop it onto another page — confirm order updates correctly
4. Confirm rotation, skip, and gap-zone clicks still work normally (not accidentally starting a drag)
5. Add split points and drag pages across them — confirm section headers shift appropriately
6. Run `npm run tsc` in `./frontend` to confirm no type errors

